# =============================================================================
# mori — A panic aborts the process: stdout before it is printed, the run exits non-zero.
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • `panic` (the en alias of `mori`) is a fatal abort — the run ends on it and
#     the exit code is non-zero
#   • Output ordering — statements before the `panic` print normally; nothing
#     after it executes
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Expecting `panic` to be recoverable — it is not part of the `catch`
#     channel; use `throw`/`iace` for recoverable failure paths
#
# See also: mori, cape
# =============================================================================

main {
    print "before"
    panic "boom"
    print "after"
}
